# Buttons and forms

Use native Home Assistant form components wherever they already provide the required behaviour. Apply civica typography, boundary, focus and colour tokens consistently.


## Choose the control by its meaning

This page is the forms and interaction overview. The individual components own their markup and behaviour:

| User intent | Use | Meaning |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Request an operation or submit answers | [Button](buttons.html) | A request, with pending and outcome feedback |
| Choose several independent options | [Checkboxes](checkboxes.html) | Each option has its own selected state |
| Choose one answer from a short set | [Radios](radios.html) | One mutually exclusive selection |
| Choose from a longer set | [Select](select.html) | One labelled saved or draft value |
| Change a supported live two-state device | Its native switch/control; see [device controls](devices.html) | Reported device state remains separate from an accepted command |
| Move to another page or detail view | [Navigation link](navigation.html) | A destination, without a device command |

State whether a preference applies immediately or on a named submit action. Do not invent a Save step for an immediate theme setting. A checkbox selecting a device for a later task must not also operate that device. Keep validation and retained-answer rules here, and use the component owner for detailed interaction requirements.

